    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d147">

                <pb facs="0204" n="186" sameAs="frus:frus1946v11/pg186"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">835.796/1–846: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Chargé in Argentina</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Cabot</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">restricted</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">us urgent</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1946-01-17T20:00:00-05:00">January 17, 1946—8
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>100. Urtel 80, Jan. 8.<anchor n="12"
                        xml:id="d147-f1"/>
                    LADE,<anchor n="13" xml:id="d147-f2"/> though
                    engaged in commercial operations, is army-owned and operated. Any US equipment
                    made available to it at this time, aside from strengthening striking potential
                    of army, which admittedly may be strengthened from other sources, will be
                    capitalized by Peronistas as best possible evidence our pusillanimous
                    policy.</p>
                <p>It is evident that Air Secretary<anchor n="14" xml:id="d147-f3"/> is playing US
                    against British.…</p>
                <p>Ranking United Aircraft officials have discussed situation thoroughly with Dept
                    and are sympathetic Dept viewpoint.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Acheson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d147-f1" n="12" xml:id="d147-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d147-f2" n="13" xml:id="d147-f2-content">
                <p>Líneas Aéreas del Estado, an Argentine airline.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d147-f3" n="14" xml:id="d147-f3-content">
                <p>Brig. Gen. Bartolome de la Colina.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
